{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1397491-how-do-you-learn-all-language-families-2nd-ed-home-brew-solutions","id":1397491,"title":"How do you learn all Language Families? (2nd Ed) -Home-brew solutions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-19T04:21:49-07:00","id":1397491,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon11.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How do you learn all Language Families? (2nd Ed) -Home-brew solutions?","content":"If you have Linguistics 5 you will have 6 Language Families (plus 25 Tribal Tongues). There are 9 total spoken throughout Creation &amp; other worlds.<br /> <br /> If you want a PC who can talk to anyone, how do you modify these rules? Or is there a ruling I missed in 2nd Edition (or 2.5)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T06:09:25-07:00","id":1397496,"title":"","content":"I would just let them buy additional languages as specialties as an easy house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T12:44:21-07:00","id":1397559,"title":"","content":"That is logical.<br /> <br /> To differentiate it from Dialect Specialties, would you do each one as a 2 dot or 3rd dot Specialty?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T14:23:31-07:00","id":1397579,"title":"","content":"I would just do two-dot, because I think actually raising linguistics gave you dice, and access to charms. Additional languages are basically just flavor. I mean sure it can have actual impact, but you could also just have a charm for that if you're an Exalt. No balancing reason to have it be super expensive, or unattainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T03:45:33-07:00","id":1401084,"title":"","content":"This is brilliant work, Cheshire.<br /> <br /> It ties it all in a neat bow &amp; is very intuitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:31